<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William, Duke of Jülich-Cleves-Berg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1516">1516</a>–<a href="/years/1592">1592</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William, Duke of Jülich-Cleves-Berg, known as William the Rich, ruled the United Duchies on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-rhine">Lower Rhine</a> from 1539. His claim to Guelders led to war with Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>, who forced him to give it up by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-venlo">Treaty of Venlo</a> in 1543. He rebuilt Jülich as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> fortress town, and his sister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-cleves">Anne of Cleves</a> married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII of England</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-duke-of-julich-cleves-berg.jpg" alt="William, Duke of Jülich-Cleves-Berg" width="320" height="677" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WilhelmVvon_JuelichKleveBerg1554.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
